# PORTED.sha256 — port parity manifest (plan D24).
# SHA-256 over LF-NORMALIZED content, so it holds on Windows and Linux alike.
# Canonical source: schemas/blueprint/.shared/ in the Archally monorepo.
# Regenerate with: node scripts/port-parity.mjs --emit
#
# The `job` lines below tell the public-side verifier where each manifest prefix lives,
# relative to tools/. They are DATA, not decoration: without them the verifier would need a
# hand-maintained copy of this job list, and adding a job here while forgetting it there
# reports every file of the new job as 'missing from disk'. (Observed, 2026-07-26.)
# job quality-gate quality-gate
# job semantic-rules semantic-checker/rules
# job next-id next-id
# job coverage-check coverage-check
# job entity-query entity-query
# job doc-snippet-validate doc-snippet-validate
# job port port

